You are given a sorted integer array arr containing 1 and prime numbers, where all the integers of arr are unique. You are also given an integer k.

For every i and j where 0 <= i < j < arr.length, we consider the fraction arr[i] / arr[j].

Return the kth smallest fraction considered. Return your answer as an array of integers of size 2, where answer[0] == arr[i] and answer[1] == arr[j].

EXAMPLE:-
Input: arr = [1,2,3,5], k = 3
Output: [2,5]
Explanation: The fractions to be considered in sorted order are:
1/5, 1/3, 2/5, 1/2, 3/5, and 2/3.
The third fraction is 2/5.

//NOTE- Here all the fractions are between the range 0 to 1. On a numberline from 0 to 1 initially we have 0.5 as our mid and all the fractions will be on this very numberline only. so first we
choose an i which is from 0 and a j from 1 to the last element. Now we calculate how many fractions are smaller than mid and how many are larger or equal to mid. In the first for loop we start j 
from 1 and calculate the arr[i]/arr[j] if it is more thant mid then increment j meaning we are going to search for a smaller number ( as increasing j increases denominator and decreases the fract
ion) if this new number is smaller than mid then we stop as j next to this number will be smaller as well. Now we calculate total += n-j; the total number of fractions smaller than mid. Now we 
will increase i but keep the j at the last position. Now repeat the process , so for every number we can count the number of numbers which when made to divide the former number is less than mid.
When the number of fractions we calculated is equal to k (which are less than the mid) then that very last number is our answer.If the number of fractions are more then we decrease the mid else 
increase the mid.

class Solution {
public:
    vector<int> kthSmallestPrimeFraction(vector<int>& arr, int k) {
        int n = arr.size();
        double left = 0, right = 1, mid;
        vector<int> res;

        while (left <= right) {
            mid = left + (right - left) / 2;
            int j = 1, total = 0, num = 0, den = 0;
            double maxFrac = 0;
            for (int i = 0; i < n; ++ i) {
                while (j < n && arr[i] >= arr[j] * mid) {
                    ++j;
                }
                
                total += n - j;

                if (j < n && maxFrac < arr[i] * 1.0 / arr[j]) {
                    maxFrac = arr[i] * 1.0 / arr[j];
                    num = i; den = j;
                }
            }

            if (total == k) {
                res = {arr[num], arr[den]};
                break;
            }

            if (total > k) {
                right = mid;
            } else {
                left = mid;
            }
        }

        return res;
    }
};
